menu "Sensors Local"

    config SENSORS_LOCAL_WEATHER_EXAMPLE_DRIVER
        bool "Enable example WEATHER local sensor driver (random values, no hardware)"
        default n
        help
            Registers a fake weather sensor ("wx-example") that feeds random
            wind/temperature/humidity/pressure/rain/luminosity readings into
            the pipeline. Useful to exercise the Weather page's channel
            picker and the WX beacon encoder with no hardware attached.

            Off by default: real weather drivers (BME280, BMP180) exist, and
            these values are indistinguishable from real readings once an
            operator maps them to a Weather channel - they will be encoded
            into a WX beacon and transmitted on air. Only turn this on for
            bench testing, and turn it off again before keying a radio.

    config SENSORS_LOCAL_TELEMETRY_EXAMPLE_DRIVER
        bool "Enable example TELEMETRY local sensor driver (random values, no hardware)"
        default n
        help
            Registers a fake telemetry sensor ("tlm-example") that feeds
            random analog/digital channel values into the pipeline. Useful
            to exercise the Telemetry page's channel picker with no
            hardware attached.

            Off by default: once an operator maps one of these channels and
            enables telemetry transmission, the random values are encoded
            into telemetry beacons and sent on air, where they are
            indistinguishable from real measurements. Only turn this on for
            bench testing, and turn it off again before keying a radio.

    config SENSORS_LOCAL_BME280_DRIVER
        bool "Enable BME280 I2C WEATHER sensor driver (temperature + humidity + pressure)"
        default y
        help
            Registers a real weather sensor ("bme280") for the Bosch BME280
            digital humidity / barometric-pressure / temperature sensor over
            I2C. The slave address and the measurement settings are fixed at
            build time in BME280.h; the SDA/SCL pins are shared by every
            local sensor and come from sensors_local_i2c.h (default
            GPIO21 = SDA, GPIO22 = SCL). Those pins are excluded from every
            GPIO picker in the web admin so they cannot be reassigned to
            another peripheral. Requires the esp-idf-lib/bmp280 managed
            component, which is named after the BMP280 and drives the BME280
            as well.

            This is the default real weather sensor. It also drives the
            BMP280, the register-compatible part without the humidity
            element: the chip ID is read at bring-up, and a board carrying
            that part reports Temperature and Pressure only, with no
            Humidity source offered on the Weather page's channel picker.

    config SENSORS_LOCAL_BMP180_DRIVER
        bool "Enable BMP180 I2C WEATHER sensor driver (temperature + pressure)"
        default n
        help
            Registers a real weather sensor ("bmp180") for the Bosch BMP180
            digital barometric-pressure / temperature sensor over I2C, the
            older predecessor of the BMP280. It shares the same bus pins as
            every other local sensor (sensors_local_i2c.h), so both may be
            enabled at once: each chip answers on its own slave address.
            Requires the esp-idf-lib/bmp180 managed component.

            Off by default: turn it on only for a board actually fitted with
            a BMP180.

endmenu
